  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The plaintiffs alleged that CACI interrogators conspired with low-level military personnel to \"soften up\" detainees by subjecting them to cruel, inhuman, and degrading treatment.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385677908:249"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The plaintiffs also accused CACI interrogators of instigating and directing conduct toward detainees that violated the Geneva Conventions and the Army Field Manual.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385677908:250"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Early in the Iraq War, members of the United States Army and the Central Intelligence Agency committed a series of human rights violations and war crimes against detainees at Abu Ghraib prison.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385677908:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "On 12 November 2026, 64,718 people read the English article, about 28× the usual daily number.",
